#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:7
msgid "git - the stupid content tracker"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git' [-v | --version] [-h | --help] [-C <path>] [-c <name>=<value>]\n"
"\t    [--exec-path[=<path>]] [--html-path] [--man-path] [--info-path]\n"
"\t    [-p | --paginate | -P | --no-pager] [--no-replace-objects] "
"[--no-lazy-fetch]\n"
"\t    [--no-optional-locks] [--no-advice] [--bare] [--git-dir=<path>]\n"
"\t    [--work-tree=<path>] [--namespace=<name>] "
"[--config-env=<name>=<envvar>]\n"
"\t    <command> [<args>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Git is a fast, scalable, distributed revision control system with an "
"unusually rich command set that provides both high-level operations and full "
"access to internals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:29
msgid ""
"See linkgit:gittutorial[7] to get started, then see linkgit:giteveryday[7] "
"for a useful minimum set of commands.  The link:user-manual.html[Git User's "
"Manual] has a more in-depth introduction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:34
msgid ""
"After you mastered the basic concepts, you can come back to this page to "
"learn what commands Git offers.  You can learn more about individual Git "
"commands with \"git help command\".  linkgit:gitcli[7] manual page gives you "
"an overview of the command-line command syntax."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:38
msgid ""
"A formatted and hyperlinked copy of the latest Git documentation can be "
"viewed at https://git.github.io/htmldocs/git.html or "
"https://git-scm.com/docs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-v`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--version`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:45
msgid "Prints the Git suite version that the 'git' program came from."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:49
msgid ""
"This option is internally converted to `git version ...` and accepts the "
"same options as the linkgit:git-version[1] command. If `--help` is also "
"given, it takes precedence over `--version`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-h`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--help`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Prints the synopsis and a list of the most commonly used commands. If the "
"option `--all` or `-a` is given then all available commands are printed. If "
"a Git command is named this option will bring up the manual page for that "
"command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:61
msgid ""
"Other options are available to control how the manual page is displayed. See "
"linkgit:git-help[1] for more information, because `git --help ...` is "
"converted internally into `git help ...`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-C <path>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Run as if git was started in '<path>' instead of the current working "
"directory.  When multiple `-C` options are given, each subsequent "
"non-absolute `-C <path>` is interpreted relative to the preceding `-C "
"<path>`.  If '<path>' is present but empty, e.g. `-C \"\"`, then the current "
"working directory is left unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:73
msgid ""
"This option affects options that expect path name like `--git-dir` and "
"`--work-tree` in that their interpretations of the path names would be made "
"relative to the working directory caused by the `-C` option. For example the "
"following invocations are equivalent:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    git --git-dir=a.git --work-tree=b -C c status\n"
"    git --git-dir=c/a.git --work-tree=c/b status\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-c <name>=<value>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:82
msgid ""
"Pass a configuration parameter to the command. The value given will override "
"values from configuration files.  The <name> is expected in the same format "
"as listed by 'git config' (subkeys separated by dots)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:88
msgid ""
"Note that omitting the `=` in `git -c foo.bar ...` is allowed and sets "
"`foo.bar` to the boolean true value (just like `[foo]bar` would in a config "
"file). Including the equals but with an empty value (like `git -c foo.bar= "
"...`) sets `foo.bar` to the empty string which `git config --type=bool` will "
"convert to `false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--config-env=<name>=<envvar>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Like `-c <name>=<value>`, give configuration variable '<name>' a value, "
"where <envvar> is the name of an environment variable from which to retrieve "
"the value. Unlike `-c` there is no shortcut for directly setting the value "
"to an empty string, instead the environment variable itself must be set to "
"the empty string.  It is an error if the `<envvar>` does not exist in the "
"environment. `<envvar>` may not contain an equals sign to avoid ambiguity "
"with `<name>` containing one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:105
msgid ""
"This is useful for cases where you want to pass transitory configuration "
"options to git, but are doing so on operating systems where other processes "
"might be able to read your command line (e.g. `/proc/self/cmdline`), but not "
"your environment (e.g. `/proc/self/environ`). That behavior is the default "
"on Linux, but may not be on your system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:110
msgid ""
"Note that this might add security for variables such as `http.extraHeader` "
"where the sensitive information is part of the value, but not "
"e.g. `url.<base>.insteadOf` where the sensitive information can be part of "
"the key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--exec-path[=<path>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:116
msgid ""
"Path to wherever your core Git programs are installed.  This can also be "
"controlled by setting the GIT_EXEC_PATH environment variable. If no path is "
"given, 'git' will print the current setting and then exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--html-path`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:120
msgid ""
"Print the path, without trailing slash, where Git's HTML documentation is "
"installed and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--man-path`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:124
msgid ""
"Print the manpath (see `man(1)`) for the man pages for this version of Git "
"and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--info-path`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:128
msgid ""
"Print the path where the Info files documenting this version of Git are "
"installed and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-p`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--paginate`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:135
msgid ""
"Pipe all output into 'less' (or if set, $PAGER) if standard output is a "
"terminal.  This overrides the `pager.<cmd>` configuration options (see the "
"\"Configuration Mechanism\" section below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-P`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-pager`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:139
msgid "Do not pipe Git output into a pager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:140
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--git-dir=<path>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:144
msgid ""
"Set the path to the repository (\".git\" directory). This can also be "
"controlled by setting the `GIT_DIR` environment variable. It can be an "
"absolute path or relative path to current working directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Specifying the location of the \".git\" directory using this option (or "
"`GIT_DIR` environment variable) turns off the repository discovery that "
"tries to find a directory with \".git\" subdirectory (which is how the "
"repository and the top-level of the working tree are discovered), and tells "
"Git that you are at the top level of the working tree.  If you are not at "
"the top-level directory of the working tree, you should tell Git where the "
"top-level of the working tree is, with the `--work-tree=<path>` option (or "
"`GIT_WORK_TREE` environment variable)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:158
msgid ""
"If you just want to run git as if it was started in `<path>` then use `git "
"-C <path>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--work-tree=<path>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:166
msgid ""
"Set the path to the working tree. It can be an absolute path or a path "
"relative to the current working directory.  This can also be controlled by "
"setting the GIT_WORK_TREE environment variable and the core.worktree "
"configuration variable (see core.worktree in linkgit:git-config[1] for a "
"more detailed discussion)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--namespace=<path>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:171
msgid ""
"Set the Git namespace.  See linkgit:gitnamespaces[7] for more details.  "
"Equivalent to setting the `GIT_NAMESPACE` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--bare`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:176
msgid ""
"Treat the repository as a bare repository.  If GIT_DIR environment is not "
"set, it is set to the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-replace-objects`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:182
msgid ""
"Do not use replacement refs to replace Git objects.  This is equivalent to "
"exporting the `GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS` environment variable with any value.  "
"See linkgit:git-replace[1] for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-lazy-fetch`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:189
msgid ""
"Do not fetch missing objects from the promisor remote on demand.  Useful "
"together with `git cat-file -e <object>` to see if the object is locally "
"available.  This is equivalent to setting the `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` "
"environment variable to `1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-optional-locks`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:193
msgid ""
"Do not perform optional operations that require locks. This is equivalent to "
"setting the `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS` to `0`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-advice`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:196
msgid "Disable all advice hints from being printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--literal-pathspecs`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:201
msgid ""
"Treat pathspecs literally (i.e. no globbing, no pathspec magic).  This is "
"equivalent to setting the `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS` environment variable to "
"`1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--glob-pathspecs`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:207
msgid ""
"Add \"glob\" magic to all pathspec. This is equivalent to setting the "
"`GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS` environment variable to `1`. Disabling globbing on "
"individual pathspecs can be done using pathspec magic \":(literal)\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:208
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--noglob-pathspecs`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:213
msgid ""
"Add \"literal\" magic to all pathspec. This is equivalent to setting the "
"`GIT_NOGLOB_PATHSPECS` environment variable to `1`. Enabling globbing on "
"individual pathspecs can be done using pathspec magic \":(glob)\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--icase-pathspecs`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:217
msgid ""
"Add \"icase\" magic to all pathspec. This is equivalent to setting the "
"`GIT_ICASE_PATHSPECS` environment variable to `1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--list-cmds=<group>[,<group>...]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:228
msgid ""
"List commands by group. This is an internal/experimental option and may "
"change or be removed in the future. Supported groups are: builtins, parseopt "
"(builtin commands that use parse-options), deprecated (deprecated builtins), "
"main (all commands in libexec directory), others (all other commands in "
"`$PATH` that have git- prefix), list-<category> (see categories in "
"command-list.txt), nohelpers (exclude helper commands), alias and config "
"(retrieve command list from config variable completion.commands)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:229
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--attr-source=<tree-ish>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git.adoc:233
msgid ""
"Read gitattributes from <tree-ish> instead of the worktree. See "
"linkgit:gitattributes[5]. This is equivalent to setting the "
"`GIT_ATTR_SOURCE` environment variable."
msgstr ""

